Description: Omarchy-compatible Hyprland session for Ubuntu - applications
 Motanka is an Omarchy-compatible Hyprland layer for Ubuntu. It installs
 next to the current desktop as a separate login session, follows
 upstream Omarchy, and removes cleanly.
 .
 This optional metapackage depends on the part of upstream Omarchy's base
 package list whose packages start no system service and change no system
 policy: input methods, the GTK portal backend, the keyring, terminal and
 file tools, viewers, office and fonts, and on motanka-herdr, the herdr
 server that upstream's autostart starts.
 .
 Packages of the base list that start system services or change system
 policy (Docker, CUPS, Avahi, BlueZ, NetworkManager, ufw and others) are
 not pulled in; the Motanka helper installs them when upstream Omarchy
 asks for them.

Package: motanka-herdr
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: Omarchy-compatible Hyprland session for Ubuntu - herdr
 Motanka is an Omarchy-compatible Hyprland layer for Ubuntu. It installs
 next to the current desktop as a separate login session, follows
 upstream Omarchy, and removes cleanly.
 .
 This package ships the herdr 0.9.5 release binary, unchanged and checked
 against its pinned SHA-256 at build time, as /opt/motanka/bin/herdr.
 herdr cannot be built from the archive: its ghostty-vt crate needs Zig.
